  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe post gate refuses a fixture strike with this text:\n\n```\nFlow1: spindle housing at move 3 strikes a fixture\n```\n\nThe text does not name the struck box. When the box is the machine table (`Machine/Table`), a user with no fixture reads the refusal as a bug (#4262).\n\n## What to do\n\n- Name the struck steel in the refusal, for example `strikes Machine/Table`.\n- `fixture_struck::op_hits` already judges each fixture alone for the display. The post text can use the same result.\n- If no single box gives the hit, say that two or more boxes give it. Do not guess a name.\n\n## Found during\n\n#4262 (PR #4296). That PR fixes the phantom strike. It does not change the message.\n",
